{
  "dom_id": "step-q2953",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given that $\\sqrt[4]{u}={u}^{n},$ what is $n?$",
  "worked_solution": "In general, the $n$th root $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can also be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$ In this particular case, $n=4,$ $x=u,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{u}={u}^{1/4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${u}^{n}={u}^{1/4},$ so $n=\\frac{1}{4}.$",
